      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>Principles of Pension Revision Under Central Pay Commissions</h2>
        <p>
          In the Indian public administration framework, retirement benefits for civil servants, railway staff, posts and telecommunication cadres, and defence personnel are established on defined statutory principles. A pension is neither a bounty nor an ex-gratia remittance; as repeatedly affirmed by the Constitution Bench of the Supreme Court of India in the landmark <em>D.S. Nakara vs Union of India</em> case, it is vested deferred compensation for past services rendered to the state.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unlike working employees who benefit from annual career increments, promotions, and variable allowances, senior citizens rely primarily on their monthly basic pension and biannual adjustments in <strong>Dearness Relief (DR)</strong>. Over a ten-year duration, retail price escalation systematically erodes the real purchasing power of a fixed pension. The implementation of the <strong>8th Central Pay Commission</strong> seeks to restore baseline parity across more than 67 lakh pensioners nationwide.
        </p>
        <p>
          When utilizing our <strong>8th Pay Commission Pension Calculator</strong>, the underlying algorithm relies on established guidelines administered by the Department of Pension and Pensioners' Welfare (DoPPW):
        </p>
        <ul class="bullet-feature-list">
          <li><strong>Consolidation of Basic Pension:</strong> Multiplying existing 7th CPC basic pension figures by the approved fitment multiplier.</li>
          <li><strong>Dearness Relief (DR) Absorption:</strong> Incorporating accumulated inflation compensation directly into the new baseline, followed by a formal reset to zero percent.</li>
          <li><strong>Commutation Recovery Accounting:</strong> Deducting up to 40% of the base payout for retirees still serving the 15-year recovery tenure.</li>
          <li><strong>Super-Senior Additional Quantum:</strong> Factoring statutory age-based increments ranging from 20% to 100% for octogenarians and centenarians.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>Fitment Multiplier Modeling for Pension Calculations</h2>
        <p>
          The <strong>Fitment Factor</strong> serves as the central mathematical lever for determining the revised pension. While working employees apply this factor to their last drawn basic pay, existing retirees apply it directly to their existing monthly basic pension as recorded on their Pension Payment Order (PPO).
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the accumulated Dearness Relief under the 7th CPC expanded past the 50% threshold, the fitment factor operates not merely as an increment, but primarily as an absorption bridge. The table below illustrates the projected conversion across multiple working economic models:
        </p>

